"C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe" -Command '$bytes = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes('"'backend\\paths.py'); "'$text = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetString($bytes); $arr = $text -split "`n"; for ($i=72; $i -le 86; $i++) { $line=$arr[$i-1].TrimEnd("`r"); Write-Output ("{0,4}: {1}" -f $i, ($line | ConvertTo-Json -Compress)) }' in G:\projects\deskpet
 succeeded in 201ms:
  72: "            userdata/"
  73: "                config.toml"
  74: "                data/state.db"
  75: "                models/"
  76: "                logs/"
  77: "                skills/"
  78: ""
  79: "    The backend exe\u0027s ``Path.parent`` is `\u003cinstall\u003e/backend/`; we walk"
  80: "    upward to find a sibling ``userdata/`` directory (or its parent"
  81: "    that *should* contain one). We don\u0027t gate on a sentinel file —"
  82: "    DeskPet has no legacy users to preserve `%AppData%` state for, so"
  83: "    \"frozen ⇒ portable\" is the simpler invariant."
  84: ""
  85: "    The MSI installer\u0027s component manifest does NOT list any files"
  86: "    under ``userdata/``, so MSI uninstall leaves the entire userdata"

